<article class="env-lemma" id="01AV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01AV">Lemma <span data-tag="01AV">17.5.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. The support of a sheaf of rings is closed. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because (according to our conventions) a ring is $0$ if and only if $1 = 0$, and hence the support of a sheaf of rings is the support of the unit section. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>